          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'inquiétude is a learned borrowing from Latin inquiētūdō \"restlessness\" (EtymDB), built on quiēs \"rest\" with the negative in- (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
